WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.734 --> 00:00:08.375
Hi!

00:00:08.445 --> 00:00:09.187
I'm Ana.

00:00:09.406 --> 00:00:10.921
Welcome to 'What to Say!'

00:00:31.889 --> 00:00:34.476
Do you know what to say when you talk about your job?

00:00:34.528 --> 00:00:38.317
Listen out for useful language for talking about your job.

00:00:38.702 --> 00:00:41.132
Then, we'll practise saying the new phrases –

00:00:41.315 --> 00:00:42.706
after this.

00:01:03.004 --> 00:01:04.199
Life

00:01:04.549 --> 00:01:05.660
is

00:01:06.041 --> 00:01:06.953
hard.

00:01:09.649 --> 00:01:10.875
Business

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:12.859
is harder.

00:01:14.849 --> 00:01:15.969
I'm here

00:01:16.333 --> 00:01:17.453
to help you

00:01:17.661 --> 00:01:18.437
win.

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:25.348
Do you want to be the best?

00:01:27.457 --> 00:01:28.575
Yeah.

00:01:29.149 --> 00:01:29.903
I said,

00:01:29.957 --> 00:01:30.957
DO YOU

00:01:31.328 --> 00:01:33.453
WANT TO BE THE BEST?

00:01:36.177 --> 00:01:37.156
Yes.

00:01:37.461 --> 00:01:38.156
Good!

00:01:39.927 --> 00:01:40.687
You –

00:01:41.559 --> 00:01:43.632
what's your role in the company?

00:01:43.842 --> 00:01:45.891
I'm the head of design.

00:01:46.495 --> 00:01:49.266
I manage artists and graphic designers.

00:01:49.698 --> 00:01:50.508
Good.

00:01:53.066 --> 00:01:54.055
What about you?

00:01:55.227 --> 00:01:56.796
I'm a content producer.

00:01:56.929 --> 00:01:57.951
What does that mean?

00:01:58.771 --> 00:02:01.240
It means I'm responsible for writing.

00:02:02.154 --> 00:02:03.048
Nice.

00:02:04.013 --> 00:02:04.841
And you –

00:02:05.716 --> 00:02:06.809
what do you do?

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:09.599
Social media and marketing.

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:11.854
Do you like your job?

00:02:12.498 --> 00:02:13.580
Yeah, I love it!

00:02:14.772 --> 00:02:15.580
Good.

00:02:18.192 --> 00:02:19.346
BUT NOT

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:20.190
GOOD

00:02:20.284 --> 00:02:21.338
ENOUGH!

00:02:22.489 --> 00:02:23.326
Now listen.

00:02:24.127 --> 00:02:25.264
I'm here

00:02:25.629 --> 00:02:26.732
to make you

00:02:26.827 --> 00:02:28.014
the best.

00:02:30.507 --> 00:02:31.568
And I've got

00:02:32.511 --> 00:02:34.889
four hours to do it.

00:02:35.948 --> 00:02:37.014
Stand up!

00:02:42.319 --> 00:02:44.507
Let's all close our eyes,

00:02:48.616 --> 00:02:50.921
breathe deeply

00:02:52.193 --> 00:02:56.226
and think about these two important questions.

00:02:58.979 --> 00:02:59.991
One:

00:03:01.369 --> 00:03:04.792
What's the best part of your job?

00:03:05.542 --> 00:03:06.784
And two:

00:03:07.932 --> 00:03:10.885
Do you like the people you work with?

00:03:12.951 --> 00:03:14.865
Keep those eyes closed ...

00:03:15.053 --> 00:03:16.596
breathe deep ...

00:03:17.795 --> 00:03:19.334
and think ...

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:31.663
Hello again!

00:03:32.022 --> 00:03:35.389
I don't think Emir is enjoying the training very much.

00:03:36.117 --> 00:03:41.563
So, did you notice the useful phrases used for talking about your job?

00:03:41.844 --> 00:03:44.063
Listen to me and then repeat.

